// Two programs, on purpose.
//
// `src` must compile as browser code and nothing else: the PWA and the Capacitor shell are the
// only places it ever runs, and a stray `Buffer` or `node:crypto` that type-checks here would
// only be discovered on a device. `tests/crosscheck.test.ts` needs the exact opposite — it opens
// our envelopes with `node:crypto` and hashes with Node's HKDF, because agreeing with a second
// implementation of RFC 5869, FIPS 198 and SP 800-38D is what makes the vectors mean something.
//
// So the Node types are granted to `tests` and withheld from `src`, and `tsc -b` checks both.
